Privacy Policy
Effective Date: April 2, 2025

Chalkboard Wiz (“the Game”, “we”, “our”, or “us”) respects your privacy. This Privacy Policy outlines how we handle your data. The short version? We don’t collect any.

1. Information We Collect
We do not collect, store, or share any personal information or data from users of the Game. Your save files are made local to  your device and can be reset at any time through settings menu on the home screen or by uninstalling the Game entirely.

2. Internet Access and Third-Party Services
The Game may request access to the internet solely for the purpose of displaying advertisements. These ads are delivered through third-party providers such as Google AdMob. While we do not collect or access any data, these third parties may collect data as described in their own privacy policies.

Please refer to Google's Privacy Policy for more information on how they manage data.

3. Children’s Privacy
We do not knowingly collect any personal information from children. If you believe we have mistakenly collected such data, please contact us immediately and we will take appropriate action.

4. Data Security
Since we don’t collect any data, there’s no data for us to store or protect. However, we strive to ensure the Game remains safe to use and free of malicious activity.

5. Changes to This Policy
This privacy policy may be updated occasionally. Any changes will be reflected on this page, with the effective date updated above.

